---
import FullNavigationLayout from "../../astro/layouts/FullNavigationLayout.astro";
---

<FullNavigationLayout>
  <main class="mr-container mr-shell__main">
    <h1>Component API</h1>
    <p>
      Component classes use <code>mr-*</code> and describe presentation only.
      Optional JavaScript behavior uses <code>data-mr-*</code>. Native HTML and
      ARIA carry state whenever possible.
    </p>

    <h2>Cards</h2>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{`<article class="mr-card mr-card--positive">
  <header>Status</header>
  <p>Everything is ready.</p>
</article>`}</code></pre>

    <h2>Button variants</h2>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{`<button class="mr-button--outlined">Outline</button>
<button class="mr-button--positive">Save</button>`}</code></pre>

    <h2>Layer presentation primitives</h2>
    <p>
      Modal, drawer, and popover Layers may share the same optional content scaffold.
      The classes below are presentation only; <code>data-mr-layer</code> and native HTML
      still define behavior.
    </p>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{`<header class="mr-layer__header">
  <div class="mr-layer__heading">
    <h2 class="mr-layer__title">Title</h2>
    <p class="mr-layer__description">Supporting text.</p>
  </div>
  <button>Close</button>
</header>
<div class="mr-layer__body">...</div>
<footer class="mr-layer__actions">...</footer>`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Tooltip source templates may use <code>mr-tooltip__title</code> and
      <code>mr-tooltip__content</code>. See <a href="../layer-primitives/">modal/drawer Layers</a>
      and <a href="../popovers-tooltips/">popovers/tooltips</a> for live examples.
    </p>

    <h2>Behavior is separate</h2>
    <pre data-mr-copyable><code>{`<pre data-mr-copyable><code>npm install example</code></pre>

<button class="mr-search-trigger" data-mr-search
        data-mr-search-static-url="/search-index.json">
  Search
</button>`}</code></pre>

    <p>
      See the individual component pages for concrete markup and
      <a href="../progressive-enhancement/">progressive enhancement</a> for
      behavior/state semantics.
    </p>
  </main>
</FullNavigationLayout>
